# Walkthrough - HyTech Visa Copilot Backend Completion

We have successfully completed all the backend requirements, integrated the user profiles, checklists, and case readiness calculations, configured Groq's API support, and ran a full end-to-end verification pipeline using the candidate data.

## Changes Made

### 1. Database & Migrations Configuration
- Created [alembic.ini](file:///d:/git/visa/hytech_visa_backend/alembic.ini) in the root directory.
- Configured [migrations/env.py](file:///d:/git/visa/hytech_visa_backend/migrations/env.py) to load the dynamic PostgreSQL database connection strings from the environment, import all SQLAlchemy models, and support migration generation.
- Fixed a type mapping bug in [case.py](file:///d:/git/visa/hytech_visa_backend/app/models/case.py) where collection relationships (`documents` and `checklist_items`) were mapped as scalar relationships instead of lists due to incomplete type annotations (`Mapped[list]` changed to `Mapped[list["Document"]]`).
- Generated and applied the database tables successfully to PostgreSQL.

### 2. Groq API Support
- Added `GROQ_API_KEY`, `GROQ_API_BASE`, and `GROQ_MODEL` variables to Settings class in [config.py](file:///d:/git/visa/hytech_visa_backend/app/core/config.py) and [.env](file:///d:/git/visa/hytech_visa_backend/.env).
- Modified AI agents ([checklist_agent.py](file:///d:/git/visa/hytech_visa_backend/app/services/ai/checklist_agent.py), [eligibility_agent.py](file:///d:/git/visa/hytech_visa_backend/app/services/ai/eligibility_agent.py), [risk_agent.py](file:///d:/git/visa/hytech_visa_backend/app/services/ai/risk_agent.py)) to dynamically initialize `AsyncOpenAI` pointing to Groq's API endpoints if the Groq key is set.

### 3. Authentication & Profile Endpoints
- Implemented `GET /api/v1/auth/me` to retrieve current logged-in user profile details in [auth.py](file:///d:/git/visa/hytech_visa_backend/app/api/v1/routes/auth.py).
- Implemented `PATCH /api/v1/auth/profile` to update candidate profile information (education level, work experience, financial details, and language test scores) in [auth.py](file:///d:/git/visa/hytech_visa_backend/app/api/v1/routes/auth.py).

### 4. Checklist Endpoints
- Created `ChecklistOut` and `ChecklistUpdate` schemas in [case.py](file:///d:/git/visa/hytech_visa_backend/app/schemas/case.py).
- Implemented `GET /api/v1/cases/{case_id}/checklist` in [cases.py](file:///d:/git/visa/hytech_visa_backend/app/api/v1/routes/cases.py) to list all personalized checklist items for a visa case.
- Implemented `PATCH /api/v1/cases/{case_id}/checklist/{checklist_id}` to manually update details or status of a checklist item (e.g. waive it).

### 5. Document & Checklist Integration
- Modified [documents.py](file:///d:/git/visa/hytech_visa_backend/app/api/v1/routes/documents.py) so that uploading a document updates the corresponding checklist item's status (to `validated` if the health score >= 60, otherwise `rejected`) and links the document ID.
- Automatically recalculates the case's overall `readiness_score` based on validated mandatory documents and dynamically transitions the Case Status (e.g. to `documents` or `review`).

